Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?duck-brain=20P18:=20the=20P5=20fall=20chain=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20walk,=20FallSafe,=20stand-up,=20walk=20=E2=80=94=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?and=20the=20trunk=20height?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The P5 set (walk, stand-up and FallSafe, all at P 5 / D 0) was trained
as a chain: walk hands over to FallSafe when tilt + 0.1 s x tilt rate
passes 35 deg; FallSafe runs 2 s on a zero command; then, unless the
robot already stands, the stand-up network drives until it has stood
0.5 s (tilt under 10 deg, trunk above 105 mm); then walk again. None of
that existed here: the daemon's own fall handling goes limp and poses.

The chain is on when the set has a skill named `fallsafe` and a
standing network. The standing network is then reserved for getting up
(command magnitude and the body-pose mode no longer pick it), FallSafe
starts only by itself (robot.do refuses it), commands are zero for both,
the target filter carries on through every switch, the policy gain
holds (a network with a runtime manifest takes no standing or skill
softening of its P), and the limp-fall stands aside.

Tilt is the trunk z axis from up (projected gravity); its rate comes
from the gyro (gdot = g x w, thetadot = gdot_z / sin theta, sine floored
at 0.05). The trunk height is new: duck_control::stance, the trunk
origin above the lowest sole point along gravity, from the joint angles
and leg/sole tables generated from Pollen's MJCF (robot_walk.xml) by
duck-brain scripts/gen_stance_model.py and checked against MuJoCo
(within 0.4 mm; 116.6 mm upright at the P5 HOME).

A set must agree on the servo P/D its networks carry: a P5 network and
one without a manifest (32/40) in one set fail the load, naming the
file — old P32 networks never run at 5/0, nor P5 ones at 32/40.

The P5 tests run on the walk v2 (the redrawn model, 21.10) unless
P5_WALK names another network; P5_TRACE is that network's trace.
